# Convex usage for EchoCoach

This project uses **Convex** as the backend (reactive database + serverless functions).
Official docs: https://docs.convex.dev/home  (AI-optimized index: https://www.convex.dev/llms.txt)

## Core conventions
- Backend code lives in the `convex/` directory. Never edit `convex/_generated/` by hand — it is
  regenerated by `npx convex dev`.
- Use `query` for reads, `mutation` for writes, and `action` only for calling external/3rd-party
  services or APIs.
- Always define the data model in `convex/schema.ts` and validate every function's `args` with the
  `v` validators from `convex/values`.
- Prefer `.withIndex(...)` over `.filter(...)` for queries that can use an index; define indexes in
  the schema.
- On the client, use the hooks from `convex/react` (`useQuery`, `useMutation`) and import function
  references from `convex/_generated/api`.

## Frontend
- The app is Next.js (App Router, `src/` dir, TypeScript, Tailwind).
- The Convex client is provided via `src/app/ConvexClientProvider.tsx`, which reads
  `NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL` from `.env.local` (populated by `npx convex dev`).
